course: dictionary
lesson: 3766
title: Foggy: weather or mind?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Foggy has two meanings. The first is about weather: fog is a thick cloud near the ground, so foggy means full of fog and hard to see.
explain: The second is about the mind. When your thinking is slow and unclear, your head feels foggy. Look at the words around it: «a 2 am game ... means a yawning, foggy day at school.» Yawning is a clue that the child is tired, so foggy means slow and unclear, not wet.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. "A tired, unclear day at school" makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Foggy means full of fog, a thick cloud near the ground that makes it hard to see.
fact: Fog forms when warm, damp air cools near the ground.
fact: «A foggy morning» means a morning when fog hangs in the air.
fact: «I haven't the foggiest idea» means I don't know at all.
fact: Foggy can also describe a mind or memory that feels unclear, as in «a yawning, foggy day at school».
exercise: «The hills were hidden on a foggy morning.» What does foggy mean? | Sunny and warm | Covered in fresh snow | *Full of fog, so hard to see | Very loud and noisy
exercise: «Drivers slow down and use lights in foggy weather.» Why do drivers use their lights? | Because the car is new | *Because they cannot see far ahead | Because they want to dance
exercise: Ellie says, «I haven't the foggiest idea.» What does she mean? | She has a clear plan | She is cold and wet | She knows the answer exactly | *She has no idea at all
test: «After the late game, my brain felt foggy all morning.» What does foggy mean here? | *Slow and unclear, as if thinking is hard | Wet and cold | Bright and clear | Full of fog outside
test: Which word from «a yawning, foggy day at school» tells you the child is tired? | school | day | *yawning | foggy
exam: Which sentence uses foggy in the weather sense? | «The foggy mind forgot all the words.» | «Her foggy answer was crisp and bright.» | «He had not the foggiest idea.» | *«The foggy road was hard to see along.»
